# HARDENED 2026-09-06 ─ these two lines were the whole env story, and they only
# covered two of the filenames dotenv actually loads.
#
#   .env
#   .env.local
#
# Next reads .env, .env.local, .env.<mode> and .env.<mode>.local. Only
# apps/dashboard had its own .gitignore with a `.env*` glob; apps/admin,
# apps/marketing and apps/desktop fell through to this file, so
# `apps/admin/.env.production` — a file holding SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY —
# was a tracked file waiting for someone to type `git add -A`. Verified with
# `git check-ignore` before and after.
#
# The glob is deliberately wider than the loader: anything starting .env is
# ignored, and the *.example files are named back in. A new secret filename
# is therefore ignored by default rather than committed by default.
.env*
!.env*.example
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
